  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work in the round from the cuff upward. Chain 22 (S) / 26 (M) / 30 (L). Join and work 5 cm of dc rib cuff. Continue in plain dc rounds, placing a marker at the gusset position. Work "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "thumb-gusset-g117"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "thumb gusset"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " increases every other round until 10 gusset sts are on the marker. Place gusset sts on hold. Continue mitten tube to 18 cm. Shape "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "mitten-crown-g117"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "mitten crown"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " with dc2tog decreases. For the thumb, rejoin yarn at held sts and work a short tube. Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make 2. S: 22 sts. M: 26 sts. L: 30 sts. Crown reached at approx. 18 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials (one pair, size M)",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Aran yarn",
              "qty": "150 yards"
            },
            {
              "name": "5 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cuff"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 26 for size M. Join. Work 5 cm of fpdc/bpdc rib cuff in the round."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Palm and gusset"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Continue in dc rounds. Place marker. Inc 1 st each side of marker every 2nd round until 10 sts sit on the gusset marker. Place those 10 sts on a length of yarn. Continue in dc for 13 cm. Begin "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "mitten-crown-g117"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "crown"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " decreases."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The fingerless gloves pattern uses the same palm construction with the top left open rather than closed."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
